                "’The world is too much with us; late and soon, getting and spending, we lay waste our powers’ — Wordsworth.",
                "Here’s one: ‘Do not go gentle into that good night — rage, rage against the dying of the light.’ Dylan Thomas — so powerful.",
                "’In the middle of difficulty lies opportunity.’ Not a poem but words to live by! Do you have a favourite verse?",
